# Saved offsets and native textarea positions

The exact saved content and revision remain the search snapshot authority. Search row offsets are UTF-16 offsets in that raw decoded saved string, with the preceding LF-line source contract unchanged. Native textarea.value normalizes CRLF and bare CR to LF. Applying saved offsets directly therefore selected the wrong substring after preceding CRLF pairs. The independent frozen141 review confirmed five wrong real Chrome selections, including current-production literal controls; its source/core16 checks passed but browser/finite acceptance was false. Earlier573/78 modeled evidence remains historical and is not relabelled as native textarea acceptance.

This correction preserves existing revision, dirty-draft, search/open generation and mounted guards. Before selection it requires the text actually shown to equal fixed CRLF/bare-CR→LF normalization of the exact unchanged saved string, validates finite ordered UTF-16 offsets, and refuses endpoints inside CRLF or an astral surrogate pair. A linear pass counts collapsed CRLF pairs before each source endpoint; bare CR changes to LF without changing length. The resulting interval is applied to the actual textarea. An incompatible shown value or invalid interval receives an explicit refusal status. No backend content, source labels, revision, matching, query or worker contract changes.

Bare CR inside a saved LF-delimited line remains part of the backend's raw source line. Normalization may display another line in the textarea; existing result/status line/column labels still refer to saved-source geometry. Absolute navigation uses the mapped DOM UTF-16 interval. Saving an unedited file still captures the original raw string/revision. Actual typing uses the native textarea's normalized value as before; preserving original line endings during arbitrary edits is not newly claimed.

The old custom regex UI fixture did not normalize its value field. The correction epoch explicitly changes that fixture's textarea setter and three expected displayed strings/one endpoint pair. Saved-file assertions retain CRLF. Exact old573 source/test/raw and inverse before-images remain. New22 finite normalizing-model checks cover literal/regex LF/CRLF/bare CR/mixed endings, astral and combining prefixes, repeated matches, zero-length navigation, malformed intervals, exact shown-content mismatch, draft/revision/Close/cancel/disposal and held Save boundaries. Modeled dirty-close Cancel is not native browser evidence. Original engine/source-helper replays remain historical; matching sources are byte-identical. Actual corrected browser and independent acceptance require a separate campaign.

No vendor/original import, new dependency or static helper route. Inline normalization uses a trusted fixed pattern and linear mapping; no untrusted regex is executed on the browser main thread. Existing worker/caller budgets and documented OS/whole-process limitations remain. Production/public code and old573+plan44+review141 are unchanged by this author. Full workbench/regex/encoding parity, exhaustive semantics and universal superiority remain false.
